==Enemy==
The Red variant of [[Teacher Bun Bun]]. He has 400,000 HP and an attack power of 9,287, making him just barely stronger than the 400% Teacher Bun Bun in the [[Moon (Empire of Cats)|Moon/Iriomote]] stage of [[Empire of Cats]] Chapter 3 (399,996/9,000). He is knocked back only half as many times as his floating-only counterpart.

==Strategy==
Because he is a Red enemy, any ranged [[:Category:Anti-Red Cats|anti-Red units]] can take him out in a short time. [[:Category:Anti-Floating Cats|Anti-Floating units]] also work against him as he retains the floating trait. If you have many strong anti-Red Cats, defeating him may be easier than defeating his original variant. If you don't, it will be harder since he has half as many knockbacks as Teacher Bun Bun.

The strategy for defeating the regular Teacher Bun Bun applies to this enemy as well. Use mainly ranged attackers like [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]], [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cat]] and [[Crazed Lizard Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Dragon Cat]] and crowd-controllers like [[Fortune Teller Cat (Rare Cat)|Fortune Teller Cat]], [[Shaman Cat (Rare Cat)|Shaman Cat]] and [[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Sanzo Cat]] (must be in [[True Form]]). [[Sushi Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fried Shrimp Cat]] is very good against him as he has immense bulk against reds while Sanzo or Fortune Teller are able to permanently stall him if used properly. Almost any uber with over 200 range will work great against him, preferably with high damage multipliers ([[Thundia (Uber Rare Cat)|Thundia]], [[Mighty Drednot (Uber Rare Cat)|Mighty Drednot]], [[Pai-Pai (Uber Rare Cat)|Pai-Pai]]) or anti floating/red crowd control ([[Momotaro (Uber Rare Cat)|Momotaro]], [[Trickster Himeyuri (Uber Rare Cat)|Himeyuri]])

