==Trivia==
*His English name is a reference to [[wikipedia:J.K. Rowling|J.K. Rowling]], the author of the ''[[wikipedia:Harry Potter|Harry Potter]]'' series.
*His Japanese and Taiwanese name, Buntaro Akai (赤井ブン太郎 in JP, 赤井噴太郎 in TW), is a reference to [[wikipedia:ja:黒井文太郎|Buntaro Kuroi]] (黒井文太郎), a military journalist. Note that ''akai'' means "red" while ''kuroi'' means "black".
*His Korean name, Syeigseupimang (셰익스피망), roughly translates to "Shakespepper"; this name is a pun on Syeigseupio (셰익스피어, [[wikipedia:William Shakespeare|Shakespeare]]) that incorporates the word ''pimang'' (피망, "pepper", most likely referring to his coloration). Taken on its own, ''mang'' (망) also means "death".
*The major works credited to J.K. Bun Bun seem to be parodies of ''[[wikipedia:Crime and Punishment|Crime and Punishment]]'' (1866) and ''[[wikipedia:Pride and Prejudice|Pride and Prejudice]]'' (1813), and ''[[wikipedia:Les Misérables|Les Misérables]]'' (1862) respectively.
*He has the second-highest number of [[Pop Culture References|pop culture references]] of any character in the game (5), behind only [[Bears Be Back]] (6).
*[[Juliet Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Juliet Cat]]'s Japanese description states that J.K. Bun Bun wrote her favorite book, ''Taibatsu to Sanpatsu'' (体罰と散髪, "Corporal Punishment and Haircuts"). In her English description, it is referred to as ''Pride, Prejudice and Haircuts'', again a reference to ''Pride and Prejudice''.
*J.K. Bun Bun is slightly smaller than most other Bun Bun variants. You can see the first three side-by-side in [[Underground]], and again along with Bun Bun Symbiote in [[No More Bad Dreams]].
*Until [[Version 15.1 Update|Version 15.1]] of the English Version, J.K. Bun Bun did not have a second period in his name.

